  "reasoning": "This \"translation changes\" commit introduced the `helpText` caching field, the `reloadText()` methods across AbstractCommand and its subclasses, and the `commandParser.reload()` call in Server.java. This caching mechanism computed and stored helpText once (or on reload), which caused stale/incorrect help text (the \"/help bug\"). The fix commit f44d562a3dce completely reverts this pattern — removing `reload()`/`reloadText()` and replacing cached `helpText` with dynamic `getHelpText()` computation using a `help` field and inline translation lookup. All the specific lines removed/modified in the fix (reload(), reloadText(), helpText field, commandParser.reload() call) trace directly back to this commit that created them.",
